      "content": "The notion that trans women have a physical advantage over biological women is a myth perpetuated by those who want to maintain the status quo of male-dominated sports. In reality, the impact of hormone therapy on athletic performance is still not fully understood, and many studies have shown that trans women compete at a level comparable to their cisgender female counterparts. Moreover, the benefits of inclusion, such as increased participation and representation of underrepresented groups, far outweigh any perceived advantages of a binary system.",
